# What a hand-run leaves behind: a results file, the phase logs, and the sources
# the run generated. Useful while looking at a failure and not worth committing -
# a measurement's runs write to a temporary directory instead and delete it.
#
# Dot-prefixed so the Go toolchain skips it too: it holds generated .go files,
# and a directory named results/ inside the module breaks `go build ./...`.
.results/
